>> >> Let's assume that:
>> >> -- the altar is co-aligned;
>> >> -- you sacrify a corpse (not the Amulet);
>> >> -- the corpse is not from your own race;
>> >> -- the corpse has positive value (see below);
>> >> -- your god is not angry with you;
>> >> -- you have non-negative alignment;
>> >> -- you have non-negative luck;
>> >> -- the prayer timeout is zero (i.e. you could safely pray);
>> >> -- you are XP level 3 or more.
>>
>> >> Then you have chances 1/N to get an artifact, assuming that some
>> >> eligible artifacts remain available. N = 10 + 2*G*A, where G is
>> >> the number of gifts already obtained from your god, and A is the
>> >> number of artifacts already existing in the game.
>>
>> >> The "gift count" is the number of gifts already obtained from your
>> >> god through either an offering, or through crowning. Crowning may
>> >> result in obtention of Excalibur, Vorpal blade, Stormbringer, or a
>> >> spellbook of restore ability (for a Monk) or finger of death (for
>> >> a Wizard). Such a spellbook counts as a gift. The random
>> >> spellbooks you may get as a prayer gratification (if your god
>> >> likes you and your luck is high enough) do _not_ count as gifts
>> >> here. 
>>
>> >> The eligible artifacts are those with the same alignment as you,
>> >> and the unaligned artifacts. There are some restrictions on
>> >> Elf/Orc artifacts. Some classes always get as first offering gift
>> >> a specific artifact (which is adjusted to have the proper
>> >> alignment); a Wizard will get Magicbane.
>>
>> >> So, basically, as a Wizard, assuming that you are not a complete
>> >> rookie (i.e. XP level is 3 or more) and that you are not in bad
>> >> terms with your god, then you have 1/10th chance of obtaining
>> >> Magicbane per sacrifice (unless you got crowned). This translates
>> >> to about 65.1% chance of getting Magicbane in 10 sacrifices or
>> >> less; 87.8% chance in 20 sacrifices or less.
>>
>> >> Corpse value depends on monster difficulty, and a handful of other
>> >> special situations. Unicorns get a bonus or malus, depending on
>> >> their colour and your alignment. Corpses which are not fresh
>> >> enough get value zero. There is a malus for the corpse of a former
>> >> pet. If the value is zero, then "nothing happens". A negative
>> >> value upsets the altar god (there is a message). If the corpse is
>> >> consumed without a message stating that some deity is grumpy, then
>> >> the corpse had positive value. A positive corpse value is used to
>> >> compute how much extra luck you get, or how the prayer timeout is
>> >> reduced, but it does not matter in the artifact lottery. You can
>> >> get Magicbane with a newt.
>>
>> >> > Any help would be much appreciated, as I am eagerly awaiting
>> >> > getting my first athame after playing for over a year.
